config MT7932_FULLMAC
	tristate "Experimental J700 MT7932 fullmac wireless support"
	depends on PCI && OF && ARM64 && IOMMU_DMA
	depends on PCIE_APPLE_PIODMA_DIAG && CFG80211
	select FW_LOADER
	help
	  Native support for the built-in J700 Wi-Fi endpoint: managed
	  WPA2-CCMP station operation on 2.4 GHz and on the 5 GHz UNII-1, -2,
	  -2e and -3 channels that the regulatory domain permits. Radar (DFS)
	  channels are scanned passively but not joined.
	  Requires original firmware, own calibration and original-derived
	  country policy packages in addition to the cfg80211 regulatory database.
	  The device is probed before the root filesystem is mounted, so say M
	  unless those files are in the initramfs.
	  Requires a trained retained PCI link and a translated SID1 DMA domain.
	  Firmware, runtime DMA and calibration negotiation start automatically;
	  cfg80211 and userspace select the country and network. No test boot
	  parameters are required for ordinary station operation.
	  Once DMA pointers are published the module is pinned until hardware
	  reset. Normal unload is refused, including with active Bluetooth.
	  A failed probe reset retains the binding and DMA; a successful checked
	  reset retires ownership before releasing probe resources.
	  Other MediaTek devices and other machines are not matched.

config MT7932_RF_KUNIT_TEST
	bool "KUnit tests for MT7932 terminal RF failure" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT=y && MT7932_FULLMAC
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Exercise the driver's terminal calibration failure and startup
	  admission paths with synthetic devices, without radio hardware.
	  Check association wakeups, retained peer ownership and refusal to
	  reopen RF admission after a terminal calibration error.
